# macOS writes a custom-folder icon into a file literally named "Icon"
# followed by a carriage return. A bare "Icon" pattern does not match it,
# and neither does the usual "Icon" + two carriage returns trick, because
# this file has CRLF line endings and git eats the trailing CR as the
# terminator. A control-character class sidesteps line endings entirely,
# and unlike "Icon?" it does not also swallow Icons/ or Icon1.
Icon[[:cntrl:]]
.syncthing.*
